# Reads of one person's data that niji cannot prove safe by itself: not the
# viewer's own, not in an admin-only place, and not the person a mail is sent
# to. Each entry says, in one sentence, why the read is safe. The rule behind
# every entry is the same: a screen shows another person only what the page
# already prints in plain text for that viewer.
#
# An entry matches on file and the exact source of the read. `kind` is
# optional and pins what was reviewed: an entry with `kind: name` stops
# matching when the read turns into an email. When a read stops needing review
# (it moved behind an admin check, or was deleted) its entry goes stale and the
# check fails until the entry is removed.
#
# - file: app/views/reviews/_review.html.erb
#   code: "review.user_name"
#   kind: name
#   reason: Review#user_name is the reviewer's public display name, printed on every review.
[]
